 # Task list API specification
 
-Version: 1.2
+Version: 1.3
 
 Date: 2026-10-28
 
@@ -36,3 +36,17 @@ Requirement: screens must not be able to add malformed tasks to a list.
 also rejects a priority other than `low`, `normal`, or `high`, and validates every supplied tag. `tag`
 rejects an empty tag or one containing a space. Invalid input returns an `invalid-input` error whose
 message explains the failing field; it does not change the list.
+
+## Bulk import
+
+Requirement: teams can migrate spreadsheet tasks into a list and see every row that was not added.
+
+`importTasks(list, text)` imports one task per non-blank line of `text`. Each row must contain exactly
+three semicolon-separated fields: `title;priority;tags`. The title and priority are trimmed; an empty
+priority is the normal priority. The tags field is optional, and its non-empty tags are whitespace-
+separated. Each parsed task is added through `list.add`, so the normal title, priority, tag, and
+duplicate-title validation applies.
+
+The result is `{ imported, rejected }`. `imported` counts successful additions. `rejected` contains
+one `{ line, reason }` entry per non-blank row that has an invalid format or cannot be added, using a
+one-based physical line number. A rejected row does not prevent later rows from being imported.
